 ## The ladder — open items, simplest → most complex
 
+- `brake-aim-depth-latch` — **open, to decide** (2026-11-09): the brake plan's aim node applies `BrakeAimDepth`
+  (`BrakeAimTargetNode`), but `HasPassedBrakingTarget` still asks `BrakeTargetBaseNode`, the aim **without** the depth.
+  At the shipped `BrakeAimDepth = 0` they are the same node, so nothing moves today; raise the depth and the "past the
+  braking target" latch — which gates the slide sampling, the Gs-floor-at-aim sample and turn-in — fires earlier than
+  the plan lands. Decide: route the latch through `BrakeAimTargetNode`, or delete `BrakeAimDepth` now that the aim is
+  a speed-derived node and the depth is the only thing left of the entrance→apex blend.
+
+- `chicane-detector-revisit` — **open, owner wants it revisited soon (2026-11-09)**: the flag is set in `TrackLoader.BuildApexTable`
+  from the apex heading against the node behind and the node ahead, both past 1° **and on the same side** of it, and it is the
+  only input to `ChicaneBoost` (a flat +10 mph added to the corner and route terms, after the slope and crest factors since
+  build 1724). The owner's verdict after driving: **the detector is not good**. Read the shape before believing the name —
+  back and forward on the same side of the apex heading describes a single **bend**, while an S has them on opposite sides, so
+  the test may be firing on the wrong shape entirely rather than on a badly drawn chicane. Evidence first: the `Apex table:`
+  load line already prints `C`/`c` per corner, so one run per shipped track says what it fires on; then decide (a) whether the
+  test is the right shape, and (b) whether a speed boost belongs to that flag at all, or should scale with the corner's own
+  geometry (`DetectedRadius`, the span, the entry/exit angle difference).
+  **UPDATE (build 1742, compile-only, drive owed):** the owner's definition landed and it was the inverted test all
+  along — the flag fired when the road turned the *same* way behind and ahead of the apex, which is a bend. It now
+  fires on opposite sides, and the corner's `Node` moves to the node where the turn changes sign (LengthStart/End
+  re-cut around it), before the lane field is built, so the plan, the shape and the braking target all aim at the
+  flip. Not yet driven: watch whether `ChicaneBoost`'s +10 mph now lands on real S-bends and stops landing on bends,
+  and whether an S keeping the tightest radius of its **whole** span (the speed) while its apex is the flip is right.
+
